@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the v3 workload proveo writes per run — files, names, fields — measured against sbx 0.49.2
' covers: internal/sbx/kitv3.go
' covers: internal/sbx/kitv3_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/sbx.go (BuiltinAgents)
' covers: internal/sbx/upstream.go
' covers: internal/sbx/upstream_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/third_party/ (vendored, Apache-2.0, LICENSE beside it)
' plan: _spec/_plans/sbx-kit-v3-migration.puml (decisions Q1–Q3, launch, probes P0–P5)
'
' ── FILES AND NAMES (MEASURED P0, P4) ───────────────────────────────────────
' A local workload is a DIRECTORY; sbx registers its base name as the agent
' (SBX_AGENT). proveo names it AgentName(target) = proveo-<target>, which no
' built-in shadows. Inside: <agent>.yaml (descriptor, first line
' `# syntax=docker/sandbox-kit:3`) and <agent>.dockerfile (the recipe).
' WriteWorkloadV3 refuses:
'   * a built-in name — it "fails to register" (use-kits/). BuiltinAgents
'     follows `sbx run --help` on 0.49.2, which added devin.
'   * the stem `spec` — sbx parses spec.yaml as v2 (docker/sbx-releases #738).
'   * a recipe without FROM — a workload "MUST have content" (SPEC-v3).
'
' ── FIELDS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' "Any unrecognized field anywhere in the document is an error" (SPEC-v3
' §1.2), so WorkloadV3 holds only schemaVersion "3", displayName,
' description, kind workload, version and capabilities. Image, env, user,
' workdir and launch live in the recipe, not the descriptor (§8):
'   FROM <image>; ENTRYPOINT/CMD in exec form when the workload sets a launch.
' Typed configs cover what proveo generates: lifecycle@1 (install/startup
' hooks with user and the env names each reads — "a hook sees only what it
' declares"), network-policy@1 runtime allow/deny, port@1. Capabilities
' copied from a published kit (credential@1, volume@1, …) pass through
' CapabilityV3.Config as decoded YAML.
'
' ── UPSTREAM KITS (Q3: "prefer using upstream") ─────────────────────────────
' internal/sbx/third_party/ vendors claude, codex, cursor and opencode — each
' <agent>.yaml + <agent>.dockerfile — from UpstreamKitsRef (docker/sbx-kits-
' contrib@8b0844a, Apache-2.0; LICENSE kept beside them). A FROM never carries
' a published kit's capabilities (author/base-images/), so proveo COPIES them:
' UpstreamKitFor(target, opts) returns
'   * every capability except sbx@1 (proveo declares its own): credential@1,
'     network-policy, volume@1, agent-context, agent-skills, lifecycle@1;
'   * the recipe's ENTRYPOINT with argv0 reduced to its PATH name, so the
'     image's /opt/proveo/shims/<agent> → proveo-await-seed still runs first;
'   * the recipe's ENV minus upstreamLayoutEnv (PATH, CODEX_INSTALL_DIR: the
'     upstream image's install layout, not agent behaviour).
' Hooks it drops, each a recorded decision (plan: Q3 EXCEPTIONS):
'   * "Seed Claude bypass/trust flags" — `> ~/.claude.json` wiped the
'     persisted host copy in P6; accept_workspace_trust merges instead. A test
'     fails if a re-vendor renames it, so P6 gets re-checked.
'   * any hook naming MCP_GATEWAY_URL unless opts.MCPGateway (the egress row).
'
' ── PORTS (MEASURED P3) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' port@1 alone publishes localhost:<ephemeral>; with `-p H:P` for the same P
' sbx keeps ONE binding on H. So a workload may name a port with port@1 and
' proveo still pins H with the 1–9 prefix rule (_spec/internal/devports/dev-ports.puml).
title sbx v3 workload — what proveo writes

folder "<kit root>/proveo-<target>/" as DIR <<app>> {
  file "proveo-<target>.yaml\n# syntax=docker/sandbox-kit:3\nschemaVersion \"3\" · kind workload\ncapabilities: sbx@1, lifecycle@1, credential@1, …" as DESC
  file "proveo-<target>.dockerfile\nFROM proveo/<target>:<tag>\n[ENTRYPOINT/CMD]" as RECIPE
}
component "sbx create ./proveo-<target>\n-e K=V · -p <k>P:P" as CREATE <<host>>
component "SBX_AGENT=proveo-<target>" as AGENT <<cloud>>
DIR --> CREATE
CREATE --> AGENT : dir name = agent name
@enduml
